  "_approach": "The bassline/Niche strand folded into bass house: a hard-driving 4x4 kick with a snare backbeat (instead of a clap) reinforced by rim skips, tambourine and a swung hat lattice — built for the rapid-fire MC-led blends of Sheffield/Nottingham bassline nights. Distinct from bh_speed_garage_44's crash-topped energy by leaning on a tighter, snare-forward backbeat and tambourine instead. Ref: Melodigging's Bassline genre page (Niche/Sheffield-Nottingham lineage, swung garage percussion), MusicRadar's \"Build a bassline house beat in 4 steps\".",
